bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    wm_full_stack_demo_child_frames_hardcode_default_theme_2026-11-27, 0, "Found in review of the PixelSurface theme-stamp fix (pixel_surface_producer_frames_refused_no_theme_stamp_2026-11-26), by code read, 2026-11-27. After that fix lands the demo passes default_theme_id() as the pixel child frame's theme (examples/06_io/ui/wm_full_stack_demo.spl:216, test/03_system/wm/wm_full_stack_demo_spec.spl:342), matching the embedded Web child frame beside it, which already hardcoded default_theme_id() (demo :227, spec :353; on release/1.0.0 before the fix the Web sites are the only ones). Top-level admission (HostCompositor._set_external_web_frame_with_ownership) requires theme_id == active-or-default theme; set_external_child_frame has no theme check today, so nothing fails. If the child-frame path ever gains the same gate, these frames are refused whenever a non-default theme is active. Proposed: resolve active-or-default (active_wm_theme_id() if non-empty, else default_theme_id()) at all four sites, as the other WM specs do."
    wm_full_stack_demo_child_frames_hardcode_default_theme_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 w4-2: resolved active_wm_theme_id() with default_theme_id() fallback via _resolved_child_theme_id() at all four child-frame sites (examples/06_io/ui/wm_full_stack_demo.spl:216,227 and test/03_system/wm/wm_full_stack_demo_spec.spl:342,353). Windows host interpreter: wm_full_stack_demo_child_theme_spec 2/2 passed, unit wm_full_stack_demo_spec 2/2 passed; system wm_full_stack_demo_spec 3/6 passed (new active-theme example passed; 3 pre-existing HostCompositor pointer/minimize failures unrelated to theme)."

